        <definition>unsigned size</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>size</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Size of the object. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is set immediately after construction. A value of zero is also indicative that the object is still being constructed. Consequently, if the shared count reaches zero while the size is zero, the object is not destroyed. This can happen when constructors create shared pointers to <computeroutput>this</computeroutput>. </para>
